@node @code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution}
@section @code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution}

@vindex tlon-youtube-video-resolution

Video resolution @samp{(WIDTH . HEIGHT)} for generated videos.

The default value is @samp{(1280 . 720)} (720p). The type is a cons cell of two integers. Common resolutions:

@itemize
@item
720p: @samp{(1280 . 720)}
@item
1080p: @samp{(1920 . 1080)}
@item
1440p: @samp{(2560 . 1440)}
@item
4K (2160p): @samp{(3840 . 2160)}
@end itemize

You can change this value via the transient menu (@ref{@code{tlon-youtube-menu}}) using the ``Video Resolution'' option, which presents a predefined list of choices.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-api-key}
@section @code{tlon-youtube-api-key}

@vindex tlon-youtube-api-key

YouTube Data API v3 key for API requests.

The default value is @samp{nil}. The type is a string or @samp{nil}.

Get this from the Google Cloud Console. This key is used for read-only API operations.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-client-id}
@section @code{tlon-youtube-client-id}

@vindex tlon-youtube-client-id

OAuth 2.0 client ID for YouTube API authentication.

The default value is @samp{nil}. When @samp{nil}, the value is retrieved from @samp{auth-source-pass} using the shared Tlon email the first time a command needs it, not when the package is loaded. The type is a string or @samp{nil}.

This must be a @strong{Desktop app} client ID from the Google Cloud Console. Web application client IDs will not work with the @samp{oauth2-auto} authorization flow. See @ref{Authentication setup, , authentication setup} for details.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-client-secret}
@section @code{tlon-youtube-client-secret}

@vindex tlon-youtube-client-secret

OAuth 2.0 client secret for YouTube API authentication.

The default value is @samp{nil}. When @samp{nil}, the value is retrieved from @samp{auth-source-pass} using the shared Tlon email the first time a command needs it, not when the package is loaded. The type is a string or @samp{nil}.

Must correspond to the same Desktop app client as @code{tlon-youtube-client-id}.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-default-privacy}
@section @code{tlon-youtube-default-privacy}

@vindex tlon-youtube-default-privacy

Default privacy setting for uploaded videos.

The default value is @samp{"private"}. Valid values are @samp{"private"}, @samp{"unlisted"}, and @samp{"public"}.

This value is used as the default selection when you are prompted for a privacy setting during video upload.

