@node @code{tlon-youtube-generate-wavelength-video}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-generate-wavelength-video}

@findex tlon-youtube-generate-wavelength-video

Generate a video with an animated wavelength visualization from an audio file.

The command uses @samp{seewav} to generate the animation. You are prompted to select an audio file from the @samp{"uqbar-audio"} repository. The output video is saved in @code{paths-dir-downloads} with a @samp{.mp4} extension, using the original audio file's base name. The resolution is determined by @code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution} (@ref{@code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution}, , above}).

The process runs asynchronously. Upon successful completion, the generated video is opened externally via @code{tlon-browse-file}. If the process fails, the output buffer is displayed for debugging.

Requires the @samp{seewav} command-line tool to be installed and in your @samp{PATH}.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-generate-thumbnail}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-generate-thumbnail}

@findex tlon-youtube-generate-thumbnail

Generate a thumbnail image for a video using ImageMagick.

You are prompted for a video title and author(s). The command creates a thumbnail with:

@itemize
@item
A gradient background.
@item
The title rendered in the center using GilliusADF-Regular font.
@item
The author name(s) below the title.
@item
The Tlon/EA logo (from the @samp{"tlon.team-content"} repository) in the bottom-right corner.
@item
The URL @samp{"altruismoeficaz.net"} in the bottom-left corner.
@end itemize

The thumbnail dimensions match @code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution} and the image is rendered at 300 DPI for quality, then scaled down to the target resolution. The output is saved as @samp{thumbnail.png} in @code{paths-dir-downloads}.

Requires the @samp{magick} (ImageMagick) command-line tool and the specified font files in @samp{~/Library/Fonts/}.

@node Video upload
@section Video upload

@menu
* @code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}::
* @code{tlon-youtube-prepare-upload-command}::
@end menu

@node @code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}

@findex tlon-youtube-upload-video

Upload a video file to YouTube using the YouTube Data API v3 resumable upload method.

You are prompted for:
@itemize
@item
A video file (filtered to @samp{.mp4} files, defaulting to @code{paths-dir-downloads}).
@item
A title for the YouTube video.
@item
A description.
@item
A privacy setting (@samp{"private"}, @samp{"unlisted"}, or @samp{"public"}; defaults to @code{tlon-youtube-default-privacy}).
@item
An optional playlist to add the video to after upload (from @code{tlon-youtube-playlists}).
@end itemize

The upload uses a two-step process: an initialization request to obtain a resumable upload URL, followed by the actual file upload. Both steps use @samp{curl}. If a playlist is selected, the video is automatically added to it after a successful upload.

Requires @code{tlon-youtube-client-id} and @code{tlon-youtube-client-secret} to be configured.

@node @code{tlon-youtube-prepare-upload-command}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-prepare-upload-command}

@findex tlon-youtube-prepare-upload-command

Prepare the upload command for debugging without executing the final upload step.

This command runs the initialization step automatically to obtain an upload URL, then displays the exact @samp{curl} command needed for the video upload in a @samp{*YouTube Upload Commands*} buffer. You can copy and run this command manually in a terminal for testing. It uses the same prompts as @code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}.

