@node @code{tlon-youtube-authorize}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-authorize}

@findex tlon-youtube-authorize

Force re-authorization for YouTube API access. This is useful if the stored OAuth 2.0 tokens are invalid or have been revoked. The command triggers the @samp{oauth2-auto} re-authorization flow, which opens your browser for Google account authorization.

@node Transient menu
@section Transient menu

@menu
* @code{tlon-youtube-menu}::
@end menu

@node @code{tlon-youtube-menu}
@subsection @code{tlon-youtube-menu}

@findex tlon-youtube-menu

Display a @samp{transient} menu interface for YouTube operations. The menu provides the following groups:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Generate}: Generate wavelength video (@code{tlon-youtube-generate-wavelength-video}), generate thumbnail (@code{tlon-youtube-generate-thumbnail}).
@item
@strong{Upload}: Upload video (@code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}), upload thumbnail (@code{tlon-youtube-upload-thumbnail}), add video to playlist (@code{tlon-youtube-add-to-playlist}).
@item
@strong{Debug}: Prepare upload command (@code{tlon-youtube-prepare-upload-command}).
@item
@strong{Options}: Video resolution (@code{tlon-youtube-video-resolution}), authorize YouTube API (@code{tlon-youtube-authorize}).
@end itemize

@node Authentication setup
@chapter Authentication setup

To upload videos and thumbnails to YouTube, you must authorize the application to access your Google Account using OAuth 2.0. The authorization is handled by the @samp{oauth2-auto} library.

You @strong{must} use an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type @strong{Desktop app}. Web application client IDs will not work with this flow.

@menu
* Creating credentials::
* Authorization flow::
@end menu

@node Creating credentials
@section Creating credentials

@enumerate
@item
Go to the @uref{https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials, Credentials page} in the Google Cloud Console.
@item
Select the project you are using for Tlon.
@item
Click @strong{+ CREATE CREDENTIALS} and select @strong{OAuth client ID}.
@item
For @strong{Application type}, choose @strong{Desktop app}.
@item
Give it a name (e.g., ``Tlon Emacs Desktop App'').
@item
Click @strong{CREATE} and copy the @strong{Client ID} and @strong{Client Secret}.
@item
Configure @code{tlon-youtube-client-id} and @code{tlon-youtube-client-secret} with these values.
@end enumerate

@node Authorization flow
@section Authorization flow

Once credentials are configured, the first time you run a command that requires authentication (such as @code{tlon-youtube-upload-video}), @samp{oauth2-auto} automatically initiates the authorization flow:

@enumerate
@item
Your browser opens to Google's authorization page.
@item
Sign in and grant the requested permissions.
@item
Google redirects your browser to a local server that @samp{oauth2-auto} is listening on.
@item
The library captures the authorization code, exchanges it for tokens, and stores them securely.
@end enumerate

You should only need to authorize once. The system automatically refreshes tokens as they expire. If you need to re-authorize (e.g., after revoking access), use @code{tlon-youtube-authorize} (@ref{@code{tlon-youtube-authorize}, , above}).

